et and so for a few years  the site gave to Game of the Year awards  so while the PC side of the site placed  the ribbon on possibly the best point  and click game of all time in Grim  Fandango one young reviewer on the  console side had the goal to give at the  site's first ever 10 out of 10 to a  Nintendo 64 game a game that would  eventually win the site's console game  of the Year award for 1998 through a  viewer a young Jeff Grossman the game  The Legend of Zelda Ocarina  time 1999 saw another ten at a ten win  for the console game of the year one of  the best fighting games of all time Soul  Calibur while a young Greg Kasavin who  would later go on to design a bunch of  wonderful games in his own right handed  an 8.4 to the eventual winner of the PC  gaudy the timeless online role-playing  game  EverQuest 2000 is a bit of an  embarrassing one to be honest and home  to the only 10 at a time I think we'd  all agree shouldn't have been given a 10  at a 10 even some of the people who  worked on the site back then would agree  that this was a bit of a Mis score but  sadly we cannot change the past and the  first console game of the year of the  millennium went to the ten out of ten  earning Chrono Cross yeah I know much  more respectable was the PC winner in  The Sims a series that would go on to  sell well in excess of 125 million units  over the course of its lifetime 2001 was  the final year GameSpot gave a 2  separate Game of the Year awards the PC  side awarding throwback first-person  shooter Serious Sam the first encounter  the coveted prize beating at games such  as Max Payne and civilizations 3 while  perhaps the best 2d to 3d conversion in  videogame history the groundbreaking  Grand Theft Auto 3 walked away with the  console honors even beating at Tony  Hawk's Pro Skater 3 which grabbed a 10  out of 10 earlier that same year 2002  saw a unified award go to the GameCubes  metroid prime garnering in its standing  nine point seven review score to boot  beating out a suite of similarly lauded  games like Grand Theft Auto Vice City  battlefield 1942 the first Splinter Cell  morrowind and Jedi Knight 2 the  following year saw the second game of  the Year award for Nintendo struggling  console this time by a cel-shaded little  boy The Legend of Zelda Wind Waker  picked up on line point three and top  honors in the same year we saw Star Wars  Knights of the Old Republic I've been in  a few Game of the Year debates during my  five years here at GameSpot but even I  can't imagine how long the deliberations  must have been back in 2004 this was the  year of GTA san andreas Burnett 3 halo 2  The Sims 2  Metal Gear Solid 3 kotor 2 doom 3 farcry  and would you believe it half-life 2 so  what game could possibly be that such  stiff competition I mean it would have  to be one of the best games ever made as  genre-defining classic whose effect can  still be felt over a decade later so  maybe an HD remix of Chrono Cross  not kidding it was only bloody World of  Warcraft 2005 so the console snatched  back the gaudy after a 12-month  sabbatical and you know what for a  console that sold so badly the GameCube  has a bunch of Game of the Year awards  on GameSpot the latest and final being  the outstanding Resident Evil forum the  halfway point in this list witnessed the  arrival of the HD gaming generation so  it's no surprise that the poster boy of  the world's most popular console took  home the biggest honors 2006 as Gears of  War was the first Xbox exclusive to win  the award beating at stiff competition  from oblivion and The Legend of Zelda  Twilight Princess the following year was  a real barnburner for Game seeing the  launch of call of duty 4 modern warfare  halo 3 Bioshock Assassin's Creed on  portal but it was good ol Nintendo who  grabbed the honors again in 2007 with  the outstanding Super Mario Galaxy the  first hand out of 10 in seven years  Grand Theft Auto 4 failed to take home  the big prize in 2008 in fact it was the 